  "description": "Pursuit Geometry with Aggressive Stance\n\nIn the fixed-gear cycling community, a \"pursuit frame\" refers to a forward-leaning shape reminiscent of the time trial bikes used in the 1980s. This aerodynamically streamlined design not only looks sleek but also features a geometry optimized for stop-and-go cycling, excelling in quick acceleration. With a tendency towards a shorter wheelbase, it offers an exceptionally solid riding experience.\n\n≒KAGERO\n\nThe CURE model follows the design principles of the higher-end TYRANT BIKES KAGERO. While cost-cutting measures are applied to materials and fine finishes, it still strongly reflects the essence of the KAGERO design. Its sharp pipe shapes, unique to KAGERO and LEADER bikes, are also distinctive features.\n\nA Healthy and Aggressive Life for Everyone\n\nCURE's roots lie in the founder of LEADER, Salvador Lombroso, who battled pancreatic cancer. Inspired by a desire for everyone to enjoy a healthy and aggressive life, CURE was born. True to this vision, its compact frame shape, characterized by an aggressive forward lean, is ideal for a more aggressive street ride compared to traditional track bikes.\n\nVivid SAX BLUE Offered in a striking blue color not found in other LEADER models, it complements both black parts for a bold look and silver parts for a lighter custom appearance. It's a wonderful color that brightens your mood just by riding.\n\n*Includes front and rear brakes and pedals.",
